A||N||5||Cplensdorf||Door Ajar!!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Cplensdorf||03-12-2001||06:15 PM||||Does anybody know the setup for the door ajar dash light. (switches/locations/etc)?  Mine is LIT at all times and the three switches (trunk at latch, doors at front) check out fine.  Do the switches at the door simply turn on the lights, or are they also used for the door ajar, also?  One note, door switch on passenger door only has one white wire(12V) connected to it.(not what I see in the elect. schematic) It appears to turn lights on fine, though.  Driver's side has two (12V&Gd.)  Thoughts?  The car is an 88GT.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||03-12-2001||07:30 PM||||one of the switches is bad or the wire is damaged.<P>the A pilar switches work by grounding the wire(s) connected to them. The drivers A pilar wires are not +12V and ground tho they may appear so. One is for the ajar/courtesy circuit and the other is for the seatbelt alarm.<P>88 GT should have a 3 wire switch on the trunk latch. 1 wire is 12V, one wire is trunk light option, third wire is ajar. (4th wire in that harness, if present is V+ for power trunk which grounds thru the latch strike.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||03-12-2001||09:09 PM||||I think the door ajar switches are in the latch itself on the 88's. I swapped my 85 doors w pw and pl onto my Formula and lost the ajar light funtion. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||03-12-2001||09:30 PM||||on my 87 there is also a connector that I had to plug into the latch itself when I swapped wiring harnesses.  I believe the wires were black and brown, but dont quote me.  So, in addition to the A pillar switches, mine also has one in each latch.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||deceler8||03-13-2001||09:12 AM||||You didn't mention whether you checked the switch on the hood. That one isn't as well-protected as the others, so it may be the source of your troubles.<P>No one else has suggested it so I will...pull the "door ajar" bulb out of the inst. panel.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||03-13-2001||07:33 PM||||oh... I missed the year.... side door ajar is in the door. disconnects are the small black connectors inside the A pilar near the end of the rubber tube between the door and body. You can unplug 1 then the other to test w/o tearing apart the door. Then you at least know which door it is.<P>||||reg||1
